  "description": "HIJVAA crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C156 H112 Gd4 N12 O22,2(C2 H3 N1),2(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.561-3.951 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.34-110.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(μ3-OH)2L6(dbm)4]·2CH3CN·2CH2Cl2 (HL = 5-(4-o-hydroxybenzylidene)-8-hydroxylquinoline; dbm = 1,3-diphenyl-1,3-propanedione); C162H122Cl4Gd4N14O22. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
